<article class="env-remark" id="0BV9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BV9">Remark <span data-tag="0BV9">48.21.8</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a Noetherian scheme endowed with a dualizing complex $\omega _ S^\bullet $. In this case Lemmas <a href="/tag/0BV5" data-tag="0BV5">48.21.3</a>, <a href="/tag/0BV6" data-tag="0BV6">48.21.4</a>, <a href="/tag/0BV7" data-tag="0BV7">48.21.6</a>, and <a href="/tag/0BV8" data-tag="0BV8">48.21.7</a> are true for any morphism $f : X \to Y$ of finite type schemes over $S$ but with $f^!$ replaced by $f_{new}^!$. This is clear because in each case the proof reduces immediately to the affine case and then $f^! = f_{new}^!$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0AUE" data-tag="0AUE">48.20.9</a>. </p>
</article>